# shellcheck shell=bash
# Invocation behind output/evaluation/der_sweep2.csv, der_sweep2_summary.csv
# and der_sweep2_selection.json (the refined diarisation sweep: the
# pipeline's defaults and a 3 x 3 grid, ten cells).
#
# Job 8976362 (au_der_sweep2), 2026-10-04, account <project-a>, an NVIDIA
# L40S on htc-g066, on the AMI validation split, from the clone
# ~/paper_speech_transcription_audit_w2 at code 9cb43e3 with a clean tree,
# as its environment record and the selection's git_commit say. The
# record, environment/au_der_sweep2_8976362.txt beside the original's
# results on ARC, gives the effective parameters SPLIT=validation,
# CACHE_DIR=${DATA}/ami_cache, THRESHOLDS="0.65 0.70 0.75",
# MIN_CLUSTER_SIZES=12, MIN_DURATIONS_OFF="0.0 0.25 0.5" and
# OUTPUT_PREFIX=der_sweep2, so the job wrote the committed file names
# itself, and the selection's argv repeats them. Its log,
# logs/der_sweep_8976362.out in that clone, shows the preflight passing
# with --diarisation-required, the 18 meetings read from the timeline cache
# and ten configurations, the pipeline defaults first as cfg000. The two
# cells it shares with job 8976358 (der_sweep.env), the defaults and
# threshold 0.70 with no minimum pause, agree with that job's on every
# meeting.
#
# Job 8534792 (2026-08-10, htc-g061, code not recorded) ran this grid
# first, into .../output/evaluation/der_sweep_dev2/, before sweep_der had
# --output-prefix, so it wrote der_sweep*.csv and .json, and the "2" was
# added by hand when they were committed in 3645869. The two runs agree on
# every meeting but IB4002 (audit finding EDER-02, 2bb4224).
#
# CACHE_DIR below is the script's default at 9cb43e3, written out so that a
# later change of the default cannot change what this record reproduces.
#
# Reproduce (from the repository root on ARC), on the card type the
# original ran on:
#   ( set -a; . hpc/runs/der_sweep2.env || exit 1; set +a
#     sbatch --account='<your-project>' --gres=gpu:l40s:1 hpc/submit_der_sweep.sh )
#
# A reproduction writes to its own directory under repro/, so it cannot
# overwrite the ARC copy of the original run it is to be compared with.
# original: REPORT_DIR="${DATA}/speech_transcription_env/output/evaluation/audit2026/der/der_sweep2"
SPLIT=validation
CACHE_DIR="${DATA}/ami_cache"
THRESHOLDS="0.65 0.70 0.75"
MIN_CLUSTER_SIZES=12
MIN_DURATIONS_OFF="0.0 0.25 0.5"
OUTPUT_PREFIX=der_sweep2
REPORT_DIR="${DATA}/speech_transcription_env/output/evaluation/repro/der_sweep2"
